        <body>
            <div xml:id="d207">

                <pb facs="0539" n="453" sameAs="frus:frus1873p1v1/pg453"/>

                <head>No. 204.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Bassett to Mr. Fish</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Port au Prince, Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-11-28"><hi rendition="#italic">November</hi> 28, 1872</date>.
                        (Ree’d Dec. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 164.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send herewith (see
                    inclosure A) the translation of an editorial in “Le Peuple,” which appeared on
                    the morning of the 25th, though dated the 21st instant. I commend it to your
                    perusal.</p>
                <p>The article refers to the re-election of President Grant, and predicts as its
                    consequence the early re-opening of the question of the annexation of San
                    Domingo to the United States. I judge it to be a fair reflex of the prevailing
                    sentiment here, in regard to that event. It will be seen that to obviate this
                    annexation it suggests that steps should be taken by the Haytien government to
                    conclude “a treaty of peace, commerce, and alliance with Baez.” My impression is
                    that this idea was long ago suggested to this government. * * * * *</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>EBENEZER D. BASSETT.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d207-a1.xml" xpointer="d207-a1"/>
            </div>
